Z||000000||Deer_Slayer||01-14-2000||02:18 PM||||Until these days, I really never knew much about Fieros.  The only time I came close to one was when I was 14 and the girl driving it almost ran over me and my 4-wheeler over.  This past christmas was when we got a gold 86 SE.  It is truly my stepdad's, but I've somewhat "adopted" it.  While cleaning, and restoring it, I've learned a lot about these cars.  one thing that keep people from buying them in the past, I read, was the fact of the use of parts from other GM cars.  In my opinion, I see that as a blessing because suitable parts are easy to find in this day and age.  Also, I like the fact that they are easy to work on and major parts such as fenders don't cost an arm and a leg.  I just can't say enough about a Fiero.  Even when I drive around, I try to look for them on the roads and parked in various places.  I guess one can say that I'm very much "hooked".      ||||reg||10
